          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.111,
            0.884,
            0.169
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Midpoint Theorem:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the line joining the two midpoints of any two sides of a triangle is parallel to the third side and has half the length of the third side."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.174,
            0.881,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Converse to the Midpoint Theorem:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the line passing through the midpoint of a side of a triangle and parallel to a second side bisects the third side."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.237,
            0.88,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Medians of a triangle are concurrent and the point of concurrence, called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "centroid",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", divides each median in a 2 : 1 ratio."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.281,
            0.881,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The 4-gon formed by joining the midpoints of a given 4-gon is always a parallelogram."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.325,
            0.663,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• The plane can be tiled with any given 4-gon."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
